From 3b58675a04c4409bf3338e051d91bcdb7cfc84a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:54:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] live-topk: the decode indexer selects among the live
 positions on SM89 and SM12x

The non-paged decode indexer ran torch.topk, a sort and gathers over the graph
capacity (1,048,580 columns at ratio 1 on a 1M pool) although only the first
lens[b] columns are visible. live_topk.py builds the slots and selects on the
device-side lengths, element for element equal to the torch path, so a
captured graph stays replayable.

The one-CTA selection kernels are howl9003's SM89 contribution (#7). Added here:
rows with more than 8192 live columns (4096 candidate columns among blocks) are
selected by one CTA per 4096 (1024) columns, with the radix histograms summed
across the row's CTAs, so the cost stays below torch's at every length; the
among-blocks picks are sorted by position instead of flagged over the row; and
-inf candidates are never picked among blocks, as topk_among_blocks drops them.

On by default on compute capability 8.9 and 12.x; KT_IDX_LIVE_TOPK=0 restores
the torch path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
